{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1511170","title":"Biofilm microbial community assembly and pollutant removal in stormwater storage systems: effects of substrate material, light condition, and rainfall frequency","description":"This study investigated how substrate materials (polyethylene, cast iron, and ceramic), light conditions (light/dark), and rainfall frequency affect biofilm community assembly and water purification performance in laboratory-scale stormwater storage reactors. Eighteen treatment combinations (3 materials x 2 light conditions x 3 renewal frequencies) were operated for 42 days using stormwater collected from the Shenzhen University campus. Biofilm microbial communities were characterized by 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing (V4 region, paired-end) on the Illumina platform. The dataset comprises 18 biofilm samples with associated water quality measurements (COD, NH3-N, TN, TP) and material/light/frequency metadata.","center":"Shenzhen University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/08/11 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN62343516","Metagenome or environmental sample from biofilm metagenome","probable_urban","water_drainage","2025-08-11",2025,"CN","Guangdong",1795565,"Shenzhen","verified",22.53,113.94,"China: Shenzhen","stormwater storage reactor biofilm","anthropogenic environment [ENVO:01001117]","artificial water storage container","biofilm [ENVO:00002036]","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN62343517","Metagenome or environmental sample from biofilm metagenome","probable_urban","water_drainage","2025-08-11",2025,"CN","Guangdong",1795565,"Shenzhen","verified",22.53,113.94,"China: Shenzhen","stormwater storage reactor biofilm","anthropogenic environment [